# Rust build artefacts
/target/

# `cargo vendor` output for offline-build packaging (run/PHASE0_AUDIT.md
# section 7) — regenerable from Cargo.lock via `cargo vendor --sync ...`
# (see run/ for the exact command), ~540 MB, and only ever consumed by the
# packaged deliverable zip, never by ongoing development on this branch.
# Same reasoning as this file's existing zip/monolith exclusions below: a
# derived, large aggregate that would otherwise permanently bloat every
# future clone.
/vendor/

# Generated delivery package (git archive of the tree — circular to commit)
/huntsman_refactored.zip

# Generated monolithic whole-repo snapshot (regenerate: scripts/pack_monolith.py).
# Excluded for the same reason as the zip above — it is a derived, ~10 MiB
# aggregate of the tree, and bundling every key-detector test fixture into one
# new file trips GitHub secret-scanning push protection on the repo's own
# SYNTHETIC AWS-key fixtures (e.g. AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE in *_tests.rs).
# Also covers any compressed form (e.g. a manual `gzip`) — decompressing one
# reproduces the identical secret-scanning-triggering content, so compressing
# before commit only evades push-time scanning, not the reason for excluding
# it; a compressed copy previously slipped in this way and cost every Termux
# `git fetch --depth 1` install 2.9 MB of unused dead weight.
/HSE_MONOLITH.glm5.txt
/HSE_MONOLITH.glm5.txt.*

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
.DS_Store

# Runtime database / keys (HSE writes to $HOME, not repo, but be safe)
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.huntsman.env
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/settings.local.json
